---
import ProductLayout from '../../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';
import WhatIDid from '../../components/WhatIDid.astro';

const app = 'https://lock-in-2.ai.studio/';
const mission = 'https://app.joinhandshake.com/learn/vibe-code-an-app-10c2cab0/mission_step_cmtaoafw0000q2asmcm9sgk3u';
---
<ProductLayout
  slug="lock-in"
  eyebrow="Vibe-coding mission · Handshake × Google AI Studio"
  title="Lock In"
  tagline="A study app that turns your Canvas courses into <strong>exam-prep games</strong>, so you never have to re-prompt."
  hero="/images/lockin/logo-wide.webp"
  heroAlt="Lock In app icon: a smiling tan star waving under the words Lock In on dark olive"
  links={[['Try Lock In →', 'https://lock-in-2.ai.studio/']]}
  overview={[['Context', 'Handshake vibe-coding mission'], ['Deliverable', 'Live web app'], ['Tools', 'Gemini, Google AI Studio'], ['Team', 'Solo']]}
>
  <WhatIDid heading="From a prompt to a working app." items={[
    ['Defined the product', 'Turned my own study habit into a brief, using the <strong>AI task canvas</strong>: audience, context, role, output, constraints and task.'],
    ['Built it in Google AI Studio', `Vibe-coded a <a href="${app}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">working web app ↗</a> through the <a href="${mission}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Handshake Vibe Code an App mission ↗</a>.`],
    ['Designed the experience', 'Brand, star mascot, neutral palette and onboarding reveal, plus the <strong>problem map</strong>, <strong>navigation paths</strong> and key screens below.'],
  ]}>
    <p class="cta-row"><a class="btn" href={app} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Try Lock In ↗</a></p>
  </WhatIDid>

  <section class="chapter tinted">
    <h2>Why this problem</h2>
    <p class="pull">Every exam, I was <span class="hl">re-prompting Claude</span> to build me a study game. I wanted an app that already knew my classes.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>Problem map</h2>
    <p class="lead">Name the friction first.</p>
    <p>I grouped what slowed me down when studying with AI. Each group became a feature.</p>
    <figure class="band"><img src="/images/lockin/screen-problem-map.webp" alt="Problem map with four groups: re-prompting, inputs, relevance and motivation, each with sticky notes and a design answer" loading="lazy" /></figure>
    <div class="learn"><b>What I learned</b><p>The best feature removes the step people repeat most.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter tinted">
    <h2>The big decision</h2>
    <p class="lead">App, not a Claude skill.</p>
    <div class="band mycall">
      <h3>The question I asked myself</h3>
      <p class="pull">Couldn’t I just make a Claude skill?</p>
      <p class="pull answer">I could, but I’d still type in every exam by hand. Syncing <span class="hl">Canvas</span> lets the app pull my assignments for me.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>The prompt</h2>
    <p class="lead">A prompt is a design brief.</p>
    <p>I used what I learned about the <strong>AI task canvas</strong> to plan the whole build before writing a prompt.</p>
    <figure class="band"><img src="/images/lockin/screen-canvas.webp" alt="AI task canvas with six cards: audience, context, role, output, constraints and task, filled in for Lock In" loading="lazy" /></figure>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter tinted">
    <h2>Navigation paths</h2>
    <p class="lead">Always one clear next step.</p>
    <p>Set up once, then a <strong>daily loop</strong>. Before an exam, the <strong>forecast</strong> jumps straight into a game.</p>
    <figure class="band"><img src="/images/lockin/screen-nav-paths.webp" alt="Flow diagram: set up once (welcome, pick a source, confirm exams, semester scope), a daily loop (today, start session, game, results) and a before-exam path (forecast, play top 3 topics)" loading="lazy" /></figure>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>The screens</h2>
    <p class="lead">Calm colors, game energy.</p>
    <p>Inspired by <strong>Duolingo</strong> and <strong>Quizlet</strong>, with a <strong>neutral palette</strong> so studying feels calm, not loud.</p>
    <figure class="band"><img src="/images/lockin/intro-screens.webp" alt="Three phone screens of the Lock In intro: zoomed in on the star, zooming out to the logo, and the reveal with Start Daily Session" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The <strong>intro reveal</strong>: zoom in, zoom out, then Let’s lock in today.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="band"><img src="/images/lockin/screen-connect.webp" alt="Setup screen asking where to study from, with Sync with Canvas selected and Upload files as an option" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><strong>Set up once:</strong> sync Canvas, or upload files for any class.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="band"><img src="/images/lockin/screen-dashboard.webp" alt="Dashboard: Let's lock in today with a daily session button, upcoming exams with countdowns, and mastery rings per course" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><strong>Today:</strong> next exam, one button to start, mastery per course.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="band"><img src="/images/lockin/screen-forecast.webp" alt="Exam forecast listing likely topics with likelihood bars, professor-specific guidance, and the sources it was built from" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><strong>Forecast:</strong> likely topics, with <strong>professor-specific guidance</strong>.</figcaption></figure>
    <div class="band cols">
      <figure><img src="/images/lockin/screen-game.webp" alt="Game question applying a multi-attribute model, with four answers and feedback" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><strong>Game:</strong> questions tuned to what I don’t know yet.</figcaption></figure>
      <figure><img src="/images/lockin/screen-results.webp" alt="Results screen showing exam readiness rising from 72 to 79 percent and mastery by topic" loading="lazy" /><figcaption><strong>Results:</strong> readiness, streak and what to review.</figcaption></figure>
    </div>
    <p class="note">Screens above are concept designs I made to show the full flow. Try the live app for the real thing.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="chapter">
    <h2>What I learned</h2>
    <ol class="band takeaways-big" style="max-width:var(--text)">
      <li>A clear prompt is a clear design brief.</li>
      <li>Solve the step people repeat most.</li>
      <li>Start with one real user, then widen.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</ProductLayout>

<style>
  .cta-row { margin-top: 36px !important; }
</style>
